{
  "case_id": "2005-05-409",
  "document_hash": "90c1760a468a200bf8fcdd78bfd92d9e9a2c41d7ed74a47eb4b627f4f317c1b3",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2005-05-409",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90c1760a468a200bf8fcdd78bfd92d9e9a2c41d7ed74a47eb4b627f4f317c1b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c1760a468a-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument next in Kircher v. Putnam Funds Trust."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2005-05-409",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90c1760a468a200bf8fcdd78bfd92d9e9a2c41d7ed74a47eb4b627f4f317c1b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c1760a468a-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our position is that the general rule prohibiting appealability applies in this case for three reasons."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-05-409",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90c1760a468a200bf8fcdd78bfd92d9e9a2c41d7ed74a47eb4b627f4f317c1b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c1760a468a-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Why not?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2005-05-409",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90c1760a468a200bf8fcdd78bfd92d9e9a2c41d7ed74a47eb4b627f4f317c1b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c1760a468a-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What would be the consequence of that? Are there -- are there a lot of cases, or is this something that comes up often?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2005-05-409",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90c1760a468a200bf8fcdd78bfd92d9e9a2c41d7ed74a47eb4b627f4f317c1b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c1760a468a-0001-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is remanded."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. FREDERICK",
      "case_id": "2005-05-409",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90c1760a468a200bf8fcdd78bfd92d9e9a2c41d7ed74a47eb4b627f4f317c1b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c1760a468a-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress has decided that it shouldn't. Congress has decided that there is a paramount interest in having decisions made on their merits, which is why there is not appellate review of remand orders."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice ALITO",
      "case_id": "2005-05-409",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90c1760a468a200bf8fcdd78bfd92d9e9a2c41d7ed74a47eb4b627f4f317c1b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c1760a468a-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But aren't you -- aren't you urging a very strange result that the -- the decision on the merits of the SLUSA preclusion issue should be decided by the State courts when the whole purpose of -- of that provision was to take matters out of the"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. PERRY",
      "case_id": "2005-05-409",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90c1760a468a200bf8fcdd78bfd92d9e9a2c41d7ed74a47eb4b627f4f317c1b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c1760a468a-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "SLUSA precludes precisely what subsection (b) says it precludes, which is beyond the scope of 10b-5. For example, 10b-5 requires scienter. SLUSA has no scienter requirement. So a non-scienter-based State law claim is still precluded under SLUSA."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2005-05-409",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90c1760a468a200bf8fcdd78bfd92d9e9a2c41d7ed74a47eb4b627f4f317c1b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c1760a468a-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'm confused now. You're saying both sides agreed that section 1447(d) does not apply?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2005-05-409",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90c1760a468a200bf8fcdd78bfd92d9e9a2c41d7ed74a47eb4b627f4f317c1b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c1760a468a-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: And a Nassau County court could say, we're not going to treat that as preclusive."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2005-05-409",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90c1760a468a200bf8fcdd78bfd92d9e9a2c41d7ed74a47eb4b627f4f317c1b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c1760a468a-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PERRY: I respectfully disagree with you, Justice Ginsburg. The -- if the State court gave preclusive effect to the Federal court judgment, the preclusion question would be open to question -- the collateral estoppel question would be open to review."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2005-05-409",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90c1760a468a200bf8fcdd78bfd92d9e9a2c41d7ed74a47eb4b627f4f317c1b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c1760a468a-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: I -- I don't understand that. Why can't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2005-05-409",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90c1760a468a200bf8fcdd78bfd92d9e9a2c41d7ed74a47eb4b627f4f317c1b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c1760a468a-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PERRY: I think you would have to clarify at least that Missouri Pacific does not apply to SLUSA removals and remands, Justice Souter."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2005-05-409",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90c1760a468a200bf8fcdd78bfd92d9e9a2c41d7ed74a47eb4b627f4f317c1b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c1760a468a-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Counsel -- MR. PERRY: If the Court would like to change that law, it's -- it's up to this Court, but that's how we come to this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2005-05-409",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "90c1760a468a200bf8fcdd78bfd92d9e9a2c41d7ed74a47eb4b627f4f317c1b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c1760a468a-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Do you agree that there"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2005-05-409",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "90c1760a468a200bf8fcdd78bfd92d9e9a2c41d7ed74a47eb4b627f4f317c1b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c1760a468a-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: May I ask you one question, Mr. Frederick? Because it's important to me. Would you agree that a complaint that alleged that the defendant negligently used or employed manipulative devices and so forth would be covered by SLUSA -- would preempt it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Frederick",
      "case_id": "2005-05-409",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "90c1760a468a200bf8fcdd78bfd92d9e9a2c41d7ed74a47eb4b627f4f317c1b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c1760a468a-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FREDERICK: Yes, there would be. And there would be -- their argument about the Missouri Pacific case is wrong because what the -- what was going on there was the remand determination, not the underlying Federal right."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Frederick",
      "case_id": "2005-05-409",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "90c1760a468a200bf8fcdd78bfd92d9e9a2c41d7ed74a47eb4b627f4f317c1b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c1760a468a-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FREDERICK: That would be covered. And -- and the reason is that it is -- involved a manipulation. The wording of SLUSA involves a manipulation of -- of the security."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Frederick",
      "case_id": "2005-05-409",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "90c1760a468a200bf8fcdd78bfd92d9e9a2c41d7ed74a47eb4b627f4f317c1b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c1760a468a-0003-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FREDERICK: The district court was wrong in not anticipating what this Court held in Dabit, but it was not wrong insofar as it held that there was no subject-matter jurisdiction because this case is based on negligence and not fraud."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
